The definition of the word `establishment' in section  2(k), when analyzed, shows that it is an exhaustive  definition, and covers the following categories of  employers:
 of  (i) a corporation established by or under a Central,
 Provincial, or State Act;
 (ii) an authority or a body owned or controlled or  rt aided by the Government;
 (iii) a local authority;
 (iv) a Government company as defined in Section  617 of the Companies Act, 1956; and  (v) Departments of a Government.

